I am going to describe a situation that occurred a few weeks ago, and
so the details will be vague. Sorry about that.

During a Wizard ascension, I arrived at the Plane of Fire with a pet
Archon. There were two hostile Archons waiting for me. I am greedy,
and I had somewhere between 500 and 1000 spell points, so I simply
cast charm again and again. Meanwhile, the hostile Archons summoned
more nasties, which occasionally included more Archons.

When my spell points got low, I used a magic harp I had gotten by
polypiling. By the time I had tamed all the nearby Archons, I had
fewer than a hundred spell points left; but I had so many pet Archons
I could never be sure of the count (plus of course numerous pet
dragons and giants). So many pet Archons that I ran out of names for
them! (Archie, Reggie, Veronica, Betty, Jughead, Moose, that's as many
characters from the Archie comic strip as I can remember.)

At this point, although there were two hostile Archons off in the
distance, at least I could stay unblinded for several turns in a row;
so I confused myself and found the portal to the next Plane; and I
applied my unicorn horn and charged my magic harp with a blessed
scroll -- and got 1 charge in it!

This is unfair! I'm willing to admit that charging used to be too
strong, but the Dev Team has gone overboard with it, making charging
way too feeble. I protest!

The portal was fairly close; I moved a step or two closer, used my
magic whistle, and very amusingly, sent a dozen pets through to the
next level including two or three Archons! (It was the closest empty
square, so a single use of the whistle sent one pet after another to
that square.)

I only had two leashes. I whistled and whistled, trying to send
everybody through, and then I leashed two Archons and stepped through.
I lost one or two at this stage. This was the Plane of Air, and I
needed to regain lots and lots of spell points. Still, I had more than
half a dozen pet Archons and a magic whistle, so there were no
problems except -- an Archon! One of my pet Archons went from being
tame to being hostile in a single turn! I used up more spell points to
tame him back.

Air was easy, and I spent a long time on Water. The first two times I
saw the portal, I whistled some Archons through, and let the portal
hide itself underwater again. The third time, I whistled a bit,
leashed two Archons, and stepped through. I kow that I lost an Archon
or two here.

As I arrived on the Astral Plane, my blessed leash named Archie went
slack, and my blessed pet Archon named Archie, my long-time companion
who had never left my side, attacked me! Of course, I tamed him, and
with six pet Archons remaining to me (the dragons and giants all died
on one Plane or another), I easily strolled to the nearest altar which
turned out to be the right one, and the only monster I had to fight on
the Astral plane was Pestilence. My pets took care of everybody else,
or I think they would have done so if I had waited (I struck a few
blows to help them, but those blows landed on monsters or Angels or
Priests that I probably did not need to get personally involved with.)

All those pet Archons sure made things easy. You can never have too
many.

But what's this business of an Archon suddenly going hostile? Is this
a new addition they made because pet Archons are too strong? Could
they all go at once (or in quick succession as I try to tame the
first?) having that many hostile Archons could be risky for even the
most buffest protagonist, don't you think?

Can you have too many pet Archons?

